//
// Notifications pushed by KiCad on the events socket.
//
// Next to the request/reply socket, the API server listens on a publish/subscribe (nng pub0)
// socket whose URL is reported by GetServerInfo.  Every message on that socket is one serialized
// Event.  Events are fire-and-forget: a subscriber that connects late, or that cannot keep up,
// misses events, so clients should treat them as hints and re-read state through the
// request/reply socket when they need it.  The sequence number lets a client detect gaps.
//
